come  environment absolutely that was like our  non-starter that was our non-negotiable  we wanted to make sure that we had all  different versions of love on this show  um and we thought that it'd be a great  representation of how everybody can get  together and just have a good time  stefan i have to ask whose idea was it  to have your sister and brother-in-law  on the show and how quickly did you  regret having that idea  about question two of their uh of their  episodes when i realized they could go  south pretty quick  that i've been prepared mentally for the  answers that i was gonna hear  um but it was it was a no-brainer to  have him on the show that first just  because you want to be able to uh  um you know experience what a game show  is like and the questions we're gonna  ask you know with some family  but yeah i immediately regretted it for  sure  it was fine  was there like some family therapy  involved after you're like we need to  never mention this again  yeah yeah pretty much i had to think  about watching the uh the screener of  that episode uh yeah  [Laughter]  well with all of the ups and downs that  you guys have seen each other go through  and come out of the other side of  what impresses each of you about the  others stephen what impresses you about  aisha and aisha what impresses you about  stefan  i think just her overall uh her  creativity and her passion for sharing  her gifts with the world like  um you know she built it pretty much out  of nothing with an idea of just sharing  recipes out of her own kitchen  um with her own one single camera she  had and now building it was  uh i call it an empire she hates that  word but um  of  you know ways that she can bring  families together  um you know to make sure that food is  the ultimate you know  uh gathering place for family to spend  time together and to connect  and she found a lot of different ways to  share that with the world and um she  brings a  positivity to it all as well that is  